<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_trade_severity" target="ai_governance_militar::model_capability_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls and trade restrictions reduce sanctioned actors' access to advanced accelerators, cloud compute and specialized software, directly constraining their ability to train and operate large, high‑performance models and lowering their model capability level within the affected jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_militar</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_trade_severity" target="energy_supply_shock::crude_export_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded sanctions and trade controls block buyers, restrict shipping/insurance and freeze related logistics and payments, directly preventing affected producers from loading and exporting crude.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_trade_severity" target="iran_gulf_escalation::diplomatic_engagement_in" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp escalation in sanctions and trade restrictions tied to the Russia–Ukraine war polarizes international diplomacy, consumes diplomatic bandwidth and sidelines neutral mediation channels, reducing the frequency and substantive depth of diplomatic engagement aimed at de‑escalating Iran–Gulf tensions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_trade_severity" target="us_china_trade_tech::export_control_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Expansion and tightening of sanctions regimes produce new legal authorities, compliance regimes and precedent that governments and regulators quickly extend to broader export-control rules on sensitive technologies (to close re‑export loopholes and prevent sanctioned actors from acquiring dual‑use items).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_trade_tech</data>
</edge>
