<edge source="energy_supply_shock::crude_export_flow" target="ai_governance_militar::safety_engineering_effor" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher crude export flows increase revenue for oil-dependent states and defence budgets, enabling sustained or expanded funding for military AI safety R&amp;D, testing, and engineering programs; conversely drops in exports tend to force cuts in those programs.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_militar</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::crude_export_flow" target="iran_gulf_escalation::maritime_trade_disruptio" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher crude export flows normalize tanker schedules and reduce the economic and strategic incentives for interdiction or rerouting, lowering the incidence and severity of maritime trade disruptions in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::crude_export_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_ops_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Larger crude export volumes increase export revenues and foreign‑currency liquidity available to a belligerent state, easing financing of ammunition procurement, energy purchases and sustainment, which in turn supports a higher sustained military operations intensity over time.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::crude_export_flow" target="us_china_trade_tech::rare_earth_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained reductions in crude export volumes lower exporters' foreign-exchange earnings and shipping throughput, leading governments and logistics providers to prioritize energy shipments or barter deals and consequently reduce the volume of rare-earth and critical-mineral consignments along the bilateral corridor.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_trade_tech</data>
</edge>
